window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["22"]={"https://theconversation.com/safe-seats-shortchanged-why-rural-australia-bears-the-brunt-of-pork-barrelling-295342":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"c77f7d03715bcb9b57dc2cab8c038857b03b90257f1012c54716a9b1e9db4a1b","read":"https://theconversation.com/safe-seats-shortchanged-why-rural-australia-bears-the-brunt-of-pork-barrelling-295342","bytes":183657,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Safe seats, shortchanged: why rural Australia bears the brunt of pork-barrelling","by":[{"n":"William Partlett","r":"Associate Professor of Public Law, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T19:15:23Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Rural and regional Australia is chronically underfunded. From ",["healthcare","https://www.ruralhealth.org.au/publication/the-forgotten-health-spend-a-report-on-the-expenditure-deficit-in-rural-australia-2026/"]," and ",["education","https://theconversation.com/australian-students-in-rural-areas-are-not-behind-their-city-peers-because-of-socioeconomic-status-there-is-something-else-going-on-207007"]," to ",["public transport","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.retrec.2025.101650"]," and community infrastructure, living outside a capital city too often means having to settle for poorer services."]},{"k":"p","s":["Delivering services across vast and sparsely populated areas presents its own challenges. But that’s only part of the story."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another, often overlooked, factor is “ ",["pork-barrelling","https://lsj.com.au/articles/pork-barrelling-past-its-use-by-date/"],"”: the allocation of public funds not on the basis of demonstrated need, but to where they can help win votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["In practice, it means taxpayer money is often disproportionately funnelled to marginal seats the government needs to win at the next election. And most of these electoral battlegrounds are in metropolitan or outer metropolitan areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["The result is that rural and regional Australians miss out on funding that could otherwise help address chronic shortfalls in essential services."]},{"k":"h","s":["The politics of who gets what"]},{"k":"p","s":["With Victoria heading to the polls on November 28, questions about politically driven spending are back in focus."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take health, for example. In June, community advocates ",["accused","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-06-08/political-landscape-stalling-vic-hospital-funding-advocates-say/106696034"]," the Labor state government of neglecting funding for hospitals in safe electorates – including West Gippsland, Mildura and Daylesford."]},{"k":"p","s":["Advocates also pointed to the fact that in Mildura – a seat Labor hasn’t won for decades – the state Labor government spent $2 million on a hospital redevelopment feasibility study in 2021. Yet five years on, there was no funding commitment for a rebuild."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor has ",["rejected","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-06-08/political-landscape-stalling-vic-hospital-funding-advocates-say/106696034"]," the accusations. Further, this is not evidence of pork-barrelling in itself."]},{"k":"p","s":["But it raises an important question that applies at state and federal level – how do we ensure spending decisions are driven by need, not political considerations?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Taken for granted, left behind"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pork-barrelling has a long history in democracies around the world, right across the political spectrum."]},{"k":"p","s":["It can take many forms. At its most overt, the practice might involve a government promising funding for local projects in communities they want to win, particularly during an election campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["More covertly, it can take the form of bypassing competitive processes or overriding expert recommendations, again to the benefit of politically advantageous seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike outright electoral bribery, pork-barrelling isn’t explicitly against the law in Australia. Some politicians have even defended this practice as necessary “ ",["investment","https://lsj.com.au/articles/pork-barrelling-past-its-use-by-date/"],"” in local communities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Over time, however, pork-barrelling invests only in particular communities: those in marginal seats. Communities in electoral divisions already securely held by one political party – so-called “safe seats” – miss out."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no clear political advantage in directing money toward them; their political loyalty is unlikely to change."]},{"k":"p","s":["This neglect of safe seats is backed up by the numbers. A 2018 ",["analysis","https://lsj.com.au/articles/pork-barrelling-past-its-use-by-date/"]," of data collected from the Australian Electoral Commission and the Federal Department of Infrastructure show marginal electorates receive funding at a rate more than three times higher than that of safe seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Democracy’s bad eggs: corruption, pork-barrelling and abuses of power","https://theconversation.com/democracys-bad-eggs-corruption-pork-barrelling-and-abuses-of-power-229888"]]},{"k":"h","s":["The price of living outside cities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pork-barrelling puts rural Australia at a significant disadvantage. The reason is that many rural Australian divisions are safe seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["In fact, according to ",["2025 Electoral Commission data","https://www.aec.gov.au/media/files/Seat-status-fact-sheet-2025-federal-election.pdf"],", rural divisions in Queensland (Maranoa) and Victoria (Gippsland) are two of the safest Coalition seats in the house of representatives. Both are held more than 20 percentage points. Other rural seats are safe seats held by independents such as Bob Katter, federal member for Kennedy in Queensland."]},{"k":"p","s":["For rural voters, this kind of neglect can play out no matter who is in government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Labor pork-barrelling spending programs are very unlikely to direct money to these kinds of safe seats. This is because Labor is very unlikely to ever have a chance of winning these seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["Coalition pork-barrelling programs are more likely than Labor to distribute money to these rural safe seats (perhaps due to lobbying by the representative or a desire to win an independent seat). Over time, however, Coalition pork-barrelling programs are likely to focus more public money on marginal seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["For instance, the Commonwealth auditor-general ",["found","https://www.anao.gov.au/work/performance-audit/award-funding-under-the-community-sport-infrastructure-program"]," Coalition pork-barrelling in its 2020 Community Sport Infrastructure program led to “safe” and “fairly safe” Coalition-held electorates receiving “14% less funding than if funding had been awarded on the basis of assessed merit”."]},{"k":"h","s":["A concrete example"]},{"k":"p","s":["Just five days before she was critically injured in an alleged attack outside her Wangaratta electorate office, independent federal member for Indi Helen Haines met with Prime Minister Anthony Albanese to ask for additional public money to help fill the $2.7 billion health care expenditure gap between metropolitan and rural areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["A recent ",["report","https://www.ruralhealth.org.au/publication/the-forgotten-health-spend-a-report-on-the-expenditure-deficit-in-rural-australia-2026/"]," by the National Rural Health Alliance found a rural Australian receives, on average, $1,218 less in healthcare funding each year than a city resident ($138 less than last year)."]},{"k":"p","s":["This was not a new issue for Haines. Before she was elected to parliament, she had seen the effects of this funding gap as a nurse, midwife, and in healthcare research."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ABC ",["reported","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-23/helen-haines-lobbied-albanese-on-rural-health-before-attack/107298858"]," the prime minister listened to her request and noted that “a lot of people ask for money”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Recent research, however, raises questions about how fairly the Albanese government administers public spending. A September ",["report","https://publicintegrity.org.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Public-money-political-advantage.pdf"]," by independent think tank the Centre for Public Integrity analysed how the government administered a $560.9 million community infrastructure program."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the end, more than 70% of this public money was given to Labor-held electoral divisions. This included $6 million for a golf club in the prime minister’s own ",["electoral division","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/27/albanese-admits-6m-marrickville-golf-club-grant-not-to-fix-raw-sewage"],". This money could have been put to far better use in rural Australia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Another reason to end pork barrelling"]},{"k":"p","s":["The problems of pork-barrelling are well canvassed. This misuse of public money damages public trust and ",["corrupts","https://publicintegrity.org.au/pork-barrel-politics-isnt-just-about-integrity-it-is-corrupt-2/"]," democracy. It reflects a concerning ",["trend","https://theconversation.com/why-the-rise-of-cartel-parties-in-australia-threatens-our-democracy-265471"]," in which governing parties use public resources to stay in power."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022, the New South Wales state anti-corruption commission clearly stated that in some instances, pork barrelling can amount to ",["corrupt conduct","https://www.icac.nsw.gov.au/newsletter/issue60/jersey.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["More recently, the Albanese government’s community infrastructure grant program has attracted the ",["attention","https://www.smh.com.au/politics/federal/corruption-watchdog-s-interest-piqued-by-labor-s-invite-only-grants-20261022-p617r5.html"]," of the National Anti-Corruption Commission."]},{"k":"p","s":["The health of rural Australia is another reason to end this practice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Luckily, ending pork barrelling is easy to do. The government can simply commit itself to spending public money on the basis of proven need rather than political expediency."]},{"k":"p","s":["This need-based public spending will help ensure that public money is spent for public purposes rather than partisan ones. This will not only help our democracy – it will also help rural Australians."]}],"chars":6844},"https://theconversation.com/lulas-un-address-points-to-two-starkly-different-visions-of-brazilian-nationalism-ahead-of-crucial-election-290470":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"451d5634f4c5465336cf532b1649588b223279f85fbee781b0da1925a32062f1","read":"https://theconversation.com/lulas-un-address-points-to-two-starkly-different-visions-of-brazilian-nationalism-ahead-of-crucial-election-290470","bytes":194633,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Lula’s UN address points to two starkly different visions of Brazilian nationalism ahead of crucial election","by":[{"n":"Andre Pagliarini","r":"Assistant Professor of History and International Studies, Louisiana State University"}],"pub":"2026-09-22T15:24:10Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva addressed the United Nations General Assembly on Sept. 22, 2026, the Brazilian president posed a question to both an international and domestic audience: Who is to decide Brazil’s future?"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is an unusually pressing question this year. Voters in Latin America’s largest nation head to the polls on Oct. 4, marking the culmination of a campaign defined by a ",["greater degree of U.S. interference","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/01/us-trump-rubio-meddling-brazil-election"]," than any election in recent memory. Although President Donald Trump has established a ",["surprising personal rapport","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c8r8gxjxz10o"]," with the left-wing elder statesman, the U.S. administration doesn’t hide its preference for Flávio Bolsonaro. He is the son of the disgraced former President Jair Bolsonaro, who is currently ",["serving a lengthy sentence","https://apnews.com/article/jair-bolsonaro-sentence-coup-home-bf37e7ee479349cb9c7a00339e984a83"]," after being convicted of attempting to overturn the results of the 2022 election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lula has responded to U.S. pressure – which has included tariffs, sanction threats and revoked visas – by ",["making sovereignty","https://responsiblestatecraft.org/trump-brazil-tariffs/"]," a central theme of his campaign, arguing that Brazil’s political destiny must be set by Brazilians rather than what he sees as a capricious foreign power."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lula’s language has been uncompromising and often colorful. At a campaign rally outside the capital, Brasília, on Sept. 16, Lula ",["declared Brazil","https://g1.globo.com/politica/noticia/2026/09/16/lula-critica-eduardo-e-flavio-bolsonaro-de-dia-mostra-a-bandeira-nacional-e-de-noite-vai-ficar-de-quatro-para-os-estados-unidos.ghtml"]," would not tolerate politicians who “by day display the national flag and at night get on all fours for the United States.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["He has ",["denounced members","https://www.congressoemfoco.com.br/noticia/120202/lula-chama-familia-bolsonaro-de-traidora-da-patria-por-atuar-nos-eua"]," of the Bolsonaro family as traitors conspiring against the national interest in pursuit of personal gain. Such rhetoric has contributed to Lula’s ",["small but steady lead","https://www.reuters.com/3fec1b0a85a0/world/americas/brazils-lula-would-beat-bolsonaro-by-1-point-runoff-suggests-btgnexus-poll-2026-09-21/"]," in most polls."]},{"k":"p","s":["The underlying argument predates the current confrontation with Washington — and it’s also older than Lula himself, who would be sworn in at the age of 81 should he prevail in the national vote. Nationalism today might be “the master concept of the radical right,” ",["as one scholar of extremism has put it","https://doi.org/10.1093/oxfordhb/9780190274559.013.2"],", but it has never belonged exclusively to reactionaries in Brazil."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dueling notions of the nation"]},{"k":"p","s":["As I document in my new book, “ ",["Claiming the Nation","https://www.ucpress.edu/books/claiming-the-nation/hardcover"],",” Brazilian political movements both left and right throughout the 20th century competed to claim the nationalist mantle. In so doing, they argued about who was best positioned to ensure the nation lived up to its extraordinary natural potential while ascribing very different meanings to concepts like sovereignty and the national interest."]},{"k":"p","s":["One of these political traditions – which can broadly be grouped as progressive nationalist – understood national sovereignty as the capacity to determine Brazil’s economic and political development on its own terms. For its proponents, a country could not be fully independent while its resources and institutions remained excessively dependent on decisions made elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["A more conservative opposing strain of nationalism emerged after World War II in response to Brazil’s first era of mass democratic politics and presented Brazil’s failures less as a consequence of foreign dependence than of its own populist political class. This tradition viewed progressive nationalism as using promises of reform and demagogic tirades against scapegoats abroad to distract from their own corruption and irresponsibility."]},{"k":"p","s":["These two nationalist traditions offered starkly different diagnoses of Brazil’s problems and divergent political prescriptions."]},{"k":"p","s":["While Lula’s current appeals to sovereignty belong to the progressive tradition, they should not be mistaken for anti-Americanism. Brazil’s progressive nationalists have ",["historically sought","https://www.jstor.org/stable/pdf/20027635.pdf%20and%20https://www.jstor.org/stable/20455000?seq=1"]," greater room for maneuver in the international system precisely because they understood national autonomy to depend on the ability to engage the world without becoming subordinate to any single power."]},{"k":"p","s":["In that vein, Brazil has cultivated relations across ideological divides while seeking a larger voice in shaping the international order. Its efforts to assert that role, whether by pursuing a permanent seat on the U.N. Security Council or offering to mediate seemingly intractable geopolitical disputes, have ",["often been dismissed","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-latin-america-65307553"]," as ",["naive or misguided","https://www.foreignaffairs.com/brazil/what-happened-lula"],". As one ",["commentator put it","https://www.project-syndicate.org/commentary/why-lula-consorting-with-putin-and-maduro-by-andres-velasco-2023-08"],": “To behave as though Brazil could wield global power comparable to China’s, or even India’s, is pure folly.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet such dismissals overlook the foreign-policy ambitions of a large and complex nation that has historically aspired to an important global role. Sovereignty, in this formulation, is less a demand for withdrawal than a claim to political agency."]},{"k":"h","s":["The Bolsonaro reaction"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flávio Bolsonaro, by contrast, criticizes Brazilian democratic institutions – particularly the ",["Supreme Court","https://www.reutersconnect.com/item/flavio-bolsonaro-gathers-thousands-to-denounce-moraes-dictatorship-and-criticize-lula/dGFnOnJldXRlcnMuY29tLDIwMjY6bmV3c21sX09XRUZWQzU1MDIxMzM0MjE3MDAx"]," and the ",["electoral system","https://valorinternational.globo.com/politics/news/2026/07/22/flavio-bolsonaro-repeats-debunked-voting-claims-to-ambassadors.ghtml"]," – as obstacles to restoring the country’s political order."]},{"k":"p","s":["From this perspective, a closer relationship with the U.S. is perfectly compatible with national renewal. If sovereignty for Lula means defending Brazil’s freedom to chart its own course in the world, for Bolsonaristas it means reclaiming Brazil from the domestic forces he and his supporters blame for its decline."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flávio Bolsonaro’s main target is the judiciary that prosecuted and ultimately imprisoned his father. His ",["promise to free","https://www.infomoney.com.br/politica/flavio-diz-que-buscara-anistia-para-bolsonaro-ainda-durante-governo-de-transicao/"]," Jair Bolsonaro is presented not as a rejection of the rule of law but as part of a broader pledge to reform institutions that, in his telling, have exceeded their proper authority."]},{"k":"p","s":["The irony is that, notwithstanding his nationalist posturing, a Flávio Bolsonaro electoral victory would strengthen the transnational far-right current that many critics see Trump as embodying, extending the reach of a political project deeply hostile to popular sovereignty abroad."]},{"k":"h","s":["Brasília by way of New York"]},{"k":"p","s":["In his U.N. speech, Lula insisted that powerful countries cannot dictate the political choices of weaker ones. That message comes weeks after a leaked ",["confidential report","https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/colunas/monicabergamo/2026/09/abin-alerta-governo-e-tse-sobre-nivel-critico-de-escalada-de-pressao-dos-eua-contra-o-brasil-nas-eleicoes.shtml"]," from Brazil’s national intelligence service described the U.S. pressure campaign as having reached a “critical” level."]},{"k":"p","s":["Shared with the Justice Ministry and the Superior Electoral Court, Brazil’s supreme body on elections, the report indicates that, for the first time in decades, foreign influence has become serious enough to warrant the attention of the institutions charged with protecting Brazil’s political and electoral system."]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.N. was an ideal stage for Lula because it allows Brazil to reassert the principles of its independent foreign policy without signaling a retreat from international engagement."]},{"k":"p","s":["That sovereignty argument has paid political dividends at home. But the campaign has increasingly been pulled back toward another elemental fault line in Brazilian politics: corruption. The ",["crisis surrounding Banco Master","https://theconversation.com/banking-scandal-rocks-brazils-politics-and-the-countrys-presidential-election-in-october-291931"],", a failed financial institution whose owner is at the center of a sprawling investigation into fraud, money laundering and political influence, has pushed the issue to the forefront of the campaign."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ironically, while Lula is not directly implicated ",["in the scandal","https://www.reuters.com/business/finance/brazilian-top-court-unseals-probe-into-multibillion-dollar-bank-fraud-2026-09-11/"]," and Flávio Bolsonaro ",["very much is","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/may/14/flavio-bolsonaro-banker-film-jair-bolsonaro"],", the incumbent seems to be the one paying a political price for one of the largest financial scandals in Brazilian history. The more the campaign turns from sovereignty to corruption, the more vulnerable Lula becomes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nor is Lula enjoying the traditional polling bump that incumbents have ",["historically received","https://www.nexojornal.com.br/story/lula-pesquisa-atlasintel-efeito-incumbencia"]," late in the campaign. Despite relatively robust job growth and low inflation over Lula’s third term, the cost of living has been a central campaign issue dogging the president. The economy might be slowing down at exactly the wrong time for Lula’s electoral chances."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security is another top-of-mind issue that favors the challenger, ",["who has promised an approach","https://www.yahoo.com/news/us/articles/brazilian-voters-latest-eye-bukele-052451783.html"]," modeled after El Salvador’s President Nayib Bukele."]},{"k":"h","s":["The pre-election lines in the sand"]},{"k":"p","s":["For generations, Brazilian politicians have argued over whether the country’s frustrations are best explained by forces beyond its borders or by failures within them. Washington has hardly been a neutral observer."]},{"k":"p","s":["Throughout much of the 20th century, Washington ",["often quietly","https://cebri.org/revista/en/artigo/237/brazil-and-the-united-states-on-a-collision-course"]," intervened ",["to shape the political choices","https://doi.org/10.1111/blar.12518"]," available to Brazilian governments, most ",["notably in its support","https://nsarchive2.gwu.edu/NSAEBB/NSAEBB118/index.htm"]," for the 1964 coup."]},{"k":"p","s":["What is unique about this election, however, is that the U.S. is taking sides so openly and in real time through ",["hostile policy measures","https://www.wola.org/analysis/brazil-united-states-relations-election/"]," designed to put a thumb on the scale of the country’s political debate. Sovereignty, once invoked to debate development, economic dependence and Brazil’s place in the international order, has become an immediate question of de facto political authority."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flávio Bolsonaro does not reject national sovereignty. Instead, he locates threats to that sovereignty primarily inside Brazil, in institutions and political actors he regards as having thwarted his family’s political agenda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lula very pointedly locates the threat differently, emphasizing the ability to resist a foreign power’s undue exertions of leverage. They represent competing answers to the older question of what is needed for Brazil to remain master of its own destiny."]},{"k":"p","s":["On Oct. 4, Brazilians will determine which understanding of the national interest will guide their nation in an increasingly uncertain global order. The choice is whether Brazil’s sovereignty means charting its own course or accepting one charted, at least in part, somewhere else."]}],"chars":9194},"https://theconversation.com/what-the-nvidia-allegations-mean-for-canadas-growing-engagement-with-china-296388":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"ff5cec933b87d84c4977307ca4ab46eeb028842070ea1a302cd643e8efc2cc3e","read":"https://theconversation.com/what-the-nvidia-allegations-mean-for-canadas-growing-engagement-with-china-296388","bytes":187305,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"What the Nvidia allegations mean for Canada’s growing engagement with China","by":[{"n":"Kawser Ahmed","r":"Adjunct Professor, Natural Resource Institute (NRI), University of Manitoba"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T19:40:36Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Jensen Huang, the CEO of Nvidia — an American tech giant that designs and manufactures graphics processing units — ",["has resigned","https://www.ctvnews.ca/business/article/jensen-huang-resigns-as-nvidia-ceo/"]," following a controversy that exposed an uncomfortable question for western democracies: Can they pursue economic engagement with China while protecting the companies and technologies central to national security?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s renewed commercial ties with Beijing make the question a pressing one."]},{"k":"h","s":["What’s alleged"]},{"k":"p","s":[["The New York Times","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/29/us/politics/nvidia-china-jensen-huang-trump.html"]," has reported that United States intelligence officials suspected Alice Huang, a former executive at Singapore-based Megaspeed International, of passing information to Chinese intelligence. Megaspeed is an an artificial intelligence cloud infrastructure and data centre provider"]},{"k":"p","s":["The newspaper added that officials had discovered a close relationship between her and Jensen Huang, who is not related to her. On Nov. 8, ",["Nvidia announced an independent investigation","https://investor.nvidia.com/news/press-release-details/2026/Statement-from-NVIDIA-Board-of-Directors/"]," while stating that it had no reason to believe company secrets or national security were compromised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before his resignation, Jensen Huang ",["acknowledged in a message to staff that he had been unfaithful to his wife","https://www.nbcbayarea.com/news/national-international/nvidia-investigation-ceo-jensen-huang-targeted-chinese-intelligence/"],". Three U.S. House committee chairs have ",["requested a closed-door briefing","https://taiwannews.com.tw/en/news/6472904"]," with him, while ",["China rejects the spying allegations","https://www.bnnbloomberg.ca/business/international/2026/11/09/nvidia-ceo-admits-to-affair-with-woman-suspected-of-being-spy-for-china/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["The reach of foreign interference"]},{"k":"p","s":["No public finding establishes that Jensen Huang knowingly assisted foreign intelligence or that restricted information was compromised. Whether Megaspeed’s chips ",["reached Chinese users through data centres in Malaysia and Indonesia","https://www.datacenterdynamics.com/en/news/megaspeed-exec-with-close-ties-to-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-suspected-of-spying-for-china/"]," is also being investigated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Suspected technology diversion and a suspected intelligence operation are different claims, and each requires its own evidence. Singapore says its investigating Megaspeed but ",["has not investigated Alice Huang","https://www.ibtimes.com.au/megaspeed-singapore-nvidia-china-chip-investigations-1878205"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nvidia case shows that foreign interference reaches well beyond election meddling. When the target is a leading AI-chip supplier globally, the stakes extend to export controls and threatens national security."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s ",["Hogue Commission","https://foreigninterferencecommission.ca/reports"]," focused on interference in democratic institutions, while the ",["2025 CSIS public report","https://www.canada.ca/content/dam/csis-scrs/images/2025/public-report/Public%20Report_EN_2025_DIGITAL.pdf"]," goes further, identifying businesses, universities and researchers as targets of espionage and covert influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["New commission sheds light on how diaspora communities are impacted by foreign interference","https://theconversation.com/new-commission-sheds-light-on-how-diaspora-communities-are-impacted-by-foreign-interference-228681"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Foreign interference beyond elections"]},{"k":"p","s":["Commercial relationships and personal networks can provide access to sensitive information and influential decision-makers. ",["Gray-zone scholarship","https://press.armywarcollege.edu/monographs/428/"]," explains how states may pursue advantages through gradual, deniable actions that fall short of open conflict. Studies of ",["Chinese influence operations","https://warontherocks.com/2018/01/chinas-three-warfares-perspective/"]," describe the long-term cultivation of influential people and organizations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The concern arises when relationships, economic leverage and information operations combine in a co-ordinated effort to manipulate decisions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Personal relationships can also become instruments of influence. Oliver August’s 2007 book, ",["Inside the Red Mansion: On the Trail of China’s Most Wanted Man","https://www.publishersweekly.com/978-0-618-71498-8"],", traced the rise of Xiamen businessman Lai Changxing. His lavish entertainment complex, the ",["Red Mansion","https://www.latimes.com/world/la-xpm-2011-jul-23-la-fg-china-red-mansion-20110723-story.html"],", reportedly provided officials with women and other favours."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lai fled to Canada in 1999 and fought removal for about 12 years; eventually, he was ",["deported in July 2011","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/world-us-canada-14262269"],". In 2012, a Xiamen court ",["sentenced him to life in prison","https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/chinese-smuggler-who-fled-to-b-c-gets-life-sentence-1.1169243"]," for smuggling and bribery."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lai’s case involved corruption, not espionage. Still, if the Nvidia allegations are proven, they would point to a familiar technique — ",["the “honey trap”","https://www.channelnewsasia.com/east-asia/jensen-huang-affair-chinese-spy-honey-trap-6542086"]," — used in influence operations to leverage personal relationships for access to powerful people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada has experienced economic coercion first-hand. After the 2018 arrest of Huawei executive Meng Wanzhou, China restricted imports of Canadian farm products and detained Michael Kovrig and Michael Spavor. The ",["Meng Wanzhou dispute","https://www.cbc.ca/news/meng-wanzhou-huawei-kovrig-spavor-1.6188472"]," showed how commercial and diplomatic ties can become levers of pressure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Meng and the two Michaels: Why China’s hostage diplomacy failed","https://theconversation.com/meng-and-the-two-michaels-why-chinas-hostage-diplomacy-failed-168739"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Trade diversification vs. strategic rivalry"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s renewed engagement with China is understandable. American tariffs and President Donald Trump’s ",["“51st state” remarks","https://globalnews.ca/news/12031918/trump-first-comments-failed-us-canada-trade-deal/"]," have unsettled Canada’s closest economic relationship."]},{"k":"p","s":["In January 2026, Prime Minister Mark Carney announced a new strategic partnership with China. Canada introduced an annual quota of ",["49,000 Chinese electric vehicles at a 6.1 per cent tariff","https://www.international.gc.ca/trade-commerce/controls-controles/electric-vehicle-vehicule-electrique/index.aspx?lang=eng"],". Amid ",["Oshawa auto layoffs","https://news.gm.ca/en/home.detail.html/Pages/news/ca/en/2026/jan/0129_oshawa-assembly-returning-to-a-two-shift-operation.html"],", the move sparked debate about industrial policy, though the layoffs cannot simply be blamed on Chinese imports."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canadian and Chinese defence officials also ",["resumed military dialogue after eight years","https://globalnews.ca/news/12042026/indo-pacific-defence-forum-canada/"],". Canadian cabinet ministers recently ",["met Vice Premier He Lifeng","https://www.canada.ca/en/department-finance/news/2026/11/ministers-champagne-and-sidhu-deepen-canada-china-economic-ties-and-cooperation-with-vice-premier-he-lifeng.html"]," to expand economic co-operation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada aims to raise exports to China by 50 per cent by 2030. Wider market access may reduce dependence on the U.S., but it can also create vulnerabilities if security safeguards lag."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Structural realism","https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/realism-intl-relations/"],", associated with U.S. political scientist Kenneth Waltz, explains such tension: without a central authority to guarantee their security, states keep competing over sensitive technology. ",["American AI-chip export restrictions","https://www.bis.gov/press-release/department-commerce-revises-license-review-policy-semiconductors-exported-china"]," are one expression of that rivalry."]},{"k":"h","s":["The Arctic raises the stakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada has announced ",["more than $35 billion in federal northern and Arctic investments","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/03/12/prime-minister-carney-announces-ambitious-new-plan-defend-build-and"]," and a ",["defence industrial strategy","https://www.pm.gc.ca/en/news/news-releases/2026/02/17/prime-minister-carney-launches-canadas-first-defence-industrial"]," emphasizing dual-use technology, domestic innovation and secure supply chains."]},{"k":"p","s":["China’s dominance of rare-earth processing creates another dependency. The ",["International Energy Agency","https://www.iea.org/reports/rare-earth-elements/executive-summary"]," estimates China supplied 91 per cent of refined magnet rare earths in 2024. ",["Some export controls are active","https://www.spglobal.com/energy/en/news-research/latest-news/metals/110926-china-extends-rare-earth-export-suspension-to-january-2027"]," although others have been suspended."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canadian ",["Arctic security assessments","https://international.canada.ca/en/global-affairs/corporate/transparency/briefing-documents/parliamentary-committee/2025-10-30-faae"]," also identify Chinese interest in research, infrastructure and critical minerals."]},{"k":"p","s":["The risks go beyond mining. Arctic communications, remote sensing, drones and data infrastructure can serve civilian and defence purposes simutaneously. That makes partnerships valuable but sensitive. As with Nvidia, the core question is who gains access to technology, operational data and intellectual property — and on what terms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Chinese scientists are increasingly shaping the future of the Arctic amid China’s rising presence","https://theconversation.com/chinese-scientists-are-increasingly-shaping-the-future-of-the-arctic-amid-chinas-rising-presence-230509"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Engage, but protect"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada needs a practical security agenda."]},{"k":"p","s":["Governments should brief executives and researchers on recruitment and information risks. Firms should strengthen safeguards around intellectual property and supply chains and give employees confidential ways to disclose conflicts of interest and report suspected coercion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Intelligence agencies and industry associations should establish trusted channels for reporting suspicious approaches. Regulators should apply existing ",["national-security investment screening","https://ised-isde.canada.ca/site/investment-canada-act/en/investment-canada-act/guidelines/guidelines-national-security-review-investments"]," and co-ordinate oversight of dual-use technologies, while protecting legitimate academic exchange and Indigenous authority over northern projects."]},{"k":"p","s":["None of this means treating Chinese Canadians, Chinese firms, ordinary trade or employees’ private lives as suspect. It means separating lawful engagement from covert coercion, based on evidence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Nvidia investigation is unfinished and espionage has not been proved. The immediate lesson is that commercial openness needs credible safeguards. Canada can diversify its trade without trading away its capacity to make independent security decisions."]}],"chars":7320},"https://theconversation.com/uk-defence-minister-favours-backchannels-with-russia-a-diplomacy-expert-explains-why-that-would-be-fraught-with-danger-296448":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"08f3299c0899f69fc95c9b9f17fb69497eb51dc9ff9bbb7034a1dd5657e3017d","read":"https://theconversation.com/uk-defence-minister-favours-backchannels-with-russia-a-diplomacy-expert-explains-why-that-would-be-fraught-with-danger-296448","bytes":181851,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"UK defence minister favours backchannels with Russia – a diplomacy expert explains why that would be fraught with danger","by":[{"n":"David J. Wilcox","r":"Researcher in the Department of International Development, University of Birmingham"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T14:06:35Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Britain’s defence minister, Wes Streeting, has ",["said the UK","https://www.ft.com/content/4b3272a6-5d87-426a-9e2f-5428c10e7eea?syn-25a6b1a6=1"]," should establish “additional channels” of communication with Russia as a way to lower the “risk of miscalculation”. His comments come at a time of heightened tension between London and Moscow over the war in Ukraine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Backchannels have a long history in ",["diplomacy","https://theconversation.com/topics/diplomacy-79"],". They have been used by the UK as part of attempts to resolve its ",["dispute with Argentina","https://www.routledge.com/The-Official-History-of-the-Falklands-Campaign-Volume-1-The-Origins-of-the-Falklands-War/Freedman/p/book/9780415419123"]," over the Falkland Islands, as well as in ",["efforts to end","https://global.oup.com/ushe/product/deniable-contact-9780192887535?cc=gb&lang=en&"]," the Troubles in Northern Ireland. They have also ",["been used extensively","https://press.syr.edu/supressbooks/315/back-channel-negotiation/"]," in Israeli-Palestinian peace negotiations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The most well-known example of this occurred between 1992 and 1993 when key Israeli and Palestine Liberation Organization figures initiated a string of secret meetings that led to the Oslo Accords. I have explored this so-called Oslo Channel in ",["my own research","https://www.berghahnjournals.com/view/journals/israel-studies-review/38/2/isr380203.xml"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Backchannels can provide a number of benefits. First, they can act as a means of ",["dealing with uncertainty","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1571-9979.2006.00091.x"],". This includes uncertainty around the political costs of engaging in more formal diplomacy."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, they allow two sides to come together when they might be ",["willing to engage","https://direct.mit.edu/ngtn/article/34/3/297/121611/Back-Channel-Negotiations-and-Dangerous-Waiting"]," in dialogue with one another but do not want to initiate contact first to avoid being seen as desperate or weak."]},{"k":"p","s":["Backchannels can also allow different parties, such as governments or leaders of organisations, to work out what the other side’s interests and priorities are for any negotiation. And the secrecy of backchannels allows the exclusion of groups who might want to spoil such discussion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, backchannels can act as a ",["means to engage","https://doi.org/10.1163/138234008X297922"]," an adversary without preconditions and, crucially, without recognising their legitimacy or validating their demands. Russian officials, for example, regularly ",["insist","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cp89p082y2xo"]," that European countries accept Moscow’s geopolitical and security interests as legitimate and treat Russia as a “normal” state."]},{"k":"p","s":["And third, backchannels can be a means of relieving tensions by acting as a ",["“safety valve”","https://academic.oup.com/kentucky-scholarship-online/book/19800"],". The late Henry Kissinger ",["used","https://academic.oup.com/kentucky-scholarship-online/book/19800"]," confidential backchannels to ",["manage US relations","https://www.simonandschuster.co.uk/books/White-House-Years/Henry-Kissinger/9780857207104"]," with the Soviet Union while he was national security advisor to President Richard Nixon during the cold war."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, diplomatic backchannels are not without risks. Backchannels, and more importantly the contents of discussions taking place within them, can be revealed. This can ",["damage the reputations","https://doi.org/10.1163/138234008X297922"]," of those who launched them, as India’s experience shows."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 1999, India and Pakistan established a backchannel to discuss deescalating the ",["Kargil war","https://www.routledge.com/Kashmir-in-the-Shadow-of-War-Regional-Rivalries-in-a-Nuclear-Age/Wirsing/p/book/9780765610904"],". The channel was leaked to the Indian press by disgruntled officials in New Delhi’s foreign office who felt sidelined by the secret negotiations."]},{"k":"p","s":["This further ",["damaged the relationship","https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780199696475.001.0001"]," between India’s then-prime minister, Atal Bihari Vajpayee, and his Pakistani counterpart Nawaz Sharif, which had already come under pressure due to the war."]},{"k":"p","s":["Embarrassing UK politicians by revealing backchannels that undermine – even symbolically – British support for Ukraine is not inconceivable with Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["While backchannels can help reduce tensions with an adversary, ",["research","https://academic.oup.com/kentucky-scholarship-online/book/19800"]," also suggests they provide a weak foundation for longer-term changes in relations. However, Streeting’s comments appear to be less about improvising the UK’s relationship with Russia and more dealing with the immediate issue of escalation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another risk is that leaders can use backchannels to engage in what is known as ",["“channel shopping”","https://direct.mit.edu/ngtn/article/22/2/119/122141/Back-Channel-Negotiation-International-Bargaining"],". This is where an adversary looks for the alternative communication channel where they feel the most valuable concessions can be extracted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia may already be involved in a form of diplomatic channel shopping through its recent engagements with different European leaders. The German and Russian foreign ministers ",["met on the sidelines","https://www.independent.co.uk/news/ukraine-sergey-lavrov-nato-moscow-united-nations-b3056942.html"]," of the UN General Assembly in September, for example, for the first time since 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then, one month later, Finland’s President Alexander Stubb and Norwegian Prime Minister Jonas Gahr Støre held a ",["rare joint call","https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6vgj813mlelo"]," with Vladimir Putin. They said the aim of the call had been to “convey messages directly” to the Russian leader “regarding future negotiations” towards peace in Ukraine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Should backchannels be used?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peter Jones, a researcher at the University of Ottawa in Canada and practitioner in unofficial diplomatic dialogue between adversaries, has provided ",["three tests that","https://doi.org/10.1163/1871191X-12341374"]," any UK or European minister should consider when thinking about using backchannels with Russia."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, is the backchannel being used because secrecy is helpful for allowing new ways of addressing problems to be developed, or is it merely a means of managing the differences between the states?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, are those engaging in backchannels accepting and planning for its result to be put under public scrutiny? And third, is the backchannel intended to allow what would not be politically possible to take place, or is it to enable what would be illegal to take place?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The flurry of European diplomatic engagement with Russia in recent weeks may spur a fear among UK officials of missing out in diplomatic terms. However, careful and cautious use of backchannels is advised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Both the theory and history of backchannels suggest this particular diplomatic tool can be useful, but only when handled with care."]}],"chars":5197},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ireland":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"aa8895d417f01e156884757b58f3522d4c069da82d9a2744ae998280663674b1","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/ireland","bytes":57209,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ireland travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-13T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-09-04T10:53:16+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ireland/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Ireland set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Irish Embassy in the UK","https://www.ireland.ie/en/greatbritain/london/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport and ID requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are not legally required to show a passport to enter Ireland, but it may be useful to carry in case you need to prove your identity. British and Irish citizens can continue to travel freely between the UK and Ireland under the Common Travel Area."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some airlines and ferry operators have introduced, or will be introducing, a passport-only identification requirement. Check your carrier’s requirements before departure and, where necessary, travel with a valid passport. Check the ",["Ireland Citizens Information Board for guidance on acceptable ID","https://www.citizensinformation.ie/en/government-in-ireland/ireland-and-the-uk/common-travel-area-between-ireland-and-the-uk/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Irish immigration officers are entitled to ask for proof of British nationality in the course of their work."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit and remain indefinitely in Ireland under the ",["Common Travel Area rules","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/common-travel-area-guidance/common-travel-area-guidance"],". British nationals do not need a visa or residency permit to live, work or study in Ireland."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although Ireland is in the EU, it is not part of the ",["Schengen area","https://home-affairs.ec.europa.eu/policies/schengen-borders-and-visa/schengen-area_en"],", and Schengen rules do not apply."]},{"k":"p","s":["As Ireland is not in the Schengen area it is therefore not affected by the new Entry/Exit System (EES) that will be introduced in Schengen countries from 12 October 2025. You will not need to register for EES when entering Ireland. Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Ireland guide","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/109/ireland#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into and out of Ireland","https://www.revenue.ie/en/customs/individuals/info-travelling-duty-free/from-outside-eu/prohibited-restriced.aspx"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with pets"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["travelling to the EU with your pet","https://www.gov.uk/taking-your-pet-abroad/travelling-to-an-eu-country-or-northern-ireland"]," and check the ",["Irish entry requirements for pets","https://www.gov.ie/en/publication/21d40-pet-travel/#bringing-an-unaccompanied-pet-cat-dog-or-ferret-into-ireland"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Ireland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare ",["cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more","https://www.revenue.ie/en/customs/individuals/travelling-with-sending-cash/index.aspx"],". You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Ireland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Ireland cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations, political gatherings, or marches can take place with little or no warning, particularly in cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whilst most demonstrations are peaceful, they can cause disruption, including to transport routes. If you’re near areas where they are taking place, you should remain aware of what is happening around you and follow the advice of the police and local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take precautions to reduce the risk of bag-snatching or pickpocketing. Avoid carrying valuables and large amounts of money. Lock your vehicle and park where possible in a secure car park. Most incidents occur in the larger cities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of even small quantities of drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport. Do not offer to carry any items for anyone else when entering or leaving Ireland."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Ireland have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Ireland, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Ireland guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/ireland/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Ireland, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 or 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Ireland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/109/ireland#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Ireland","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/109/ireland"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK prescription to get medicines, including special food required for medical reasons, from pharmacies in Ireland. You will have to pay in full for any prescription medicine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. If you have questions, contact the ",["Irish Embassy in the UK","https://www.ireland.ie/en/greatbritain/london/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Ireland"]},{"k":"p","s":["British people who live in the UK can access state healthcare when visiting Ireland. See ",["guidance for visitors on healthcare in Ireland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-for-uk-nationals-visiting-ireland"],". FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Ireland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ireland-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living or studying in Ireland","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-ireland"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Ireland"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 or 999 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tourist SOS"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get ",["support from Tourist SOS","https://www.touristsos.ie/"]," if you are a victim of crime."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: +353 (0)1666 93 54"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Ireland"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Ireland"]," in Ireland"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Ireland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ireland-bereavement-death-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Ireland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/ireland-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/ireland/british-embassy-dublin"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ireland/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Ireland","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-ireland"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":8842,"change":"Addition of information about ID requirements for travel between the UK and Ireland under the Common Travel Area (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/midterms-aux-etats-unis-les-democrates-peuvent-ils-mettre-fin-a-la-guerre-de-trump-en-iran-296001":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"f8ce27496cd52d453e2ee20e32558a15d5bc8ecbc22013026bb3ca812b8f5867","read":"https://theconversation.com/midterms-aux-etats-unis-les-democrates-peuvent-ils-mettre-fin-a-la-guerre-de-trump-en-iran-296001","bytes":186407,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Midterms aux États-Unis : les démocrates peuvent-ils mettre fin à la guerre de Trump en Iran ?","by":[{"n":"Markus Wagner","r":"Professor of Law and Director of the UOW Transnational Law and Policy Centre, University of Wollongong"}],"pub":"2026-11-05T13:28:51Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["L’ESSENTIEL"]},{"k":"li","s":["Aux États-Unis, les démocrates, victorieux aux élections de mi-mandat, peuvent contrarier Donald Trump sur sa guerre impopulaire contre l’Iran."]},{"k":"li","s":["Au Congrès, couper les crédits de guerre exposerait toutefois les démocrates à un retour de bâton, comme pour l’Irak en 2007."]},{"k":"li","s":["La guerre en Iran a coûté aux États-Unis environ 44 milliards d’euros ; Pékin pourrait en profiter."]},{"k":"p","s":["La ",["large victoire des démocrates aux élections de mi-mandat aux États-Unis","https://theconversation.com/the-democrats-blue-tsunami-is-a-strong-repudiation-of-donald-trump-now-they-will-look-to-replicate-it-in-2028-295856"]," les met en meilleure position pour contrarier le programme du président Donald Trump. Cela vaut aussi pour sa guerre contre l’Iran, profondément impopulaire et coûteuse, qui pourrait figurer parmi leurs premières priorités."]},{"k":"p","s":["Certes, en tant que président, Trump pourra opposer son veto à toute loi visant à mettre fin à la guerre. Mais les démocrates ont encore un autre atout de poids dans leur manche : couper le financement de la guerre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Cette stratégie a toutefois ses limites. L’histoire montre que l’exercice de ce pouvoir pourrait déclencher un affrontement politique susceptible de se retourner contre eux. Et même si les démocrates parviennent à mettre fin à la guerre, ils ne pourront peut-être pas réparer les dégâts qu’elle a causés à la position des États-Unis dans le monde."]},{"k":"h","s":["Les limites de la voie législative"]},{"k":"p","s":["Les démocrates disposeront de trois options principales pour tenter de forcer la fin de la guerre contre l’Iran. Deux d’entre elles se heurtent toutefois à des limites importantes."]},{"k":"p","s":["La première option (et peut-être la plus évidente) passe par la loi. Il existe plusieurs façons de procéder. Par exemple, adopter une résolution appelant à la fin de la guerre. Le Congrès s’y est déjà essayé en juin, en adoptant une ",["résolution concurrente","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ce8j6g3v3r4o"]," (avec le soutien de certains républicains) qui enjoignait au président soit de retirer les forces états-uniennes, soit d’obtenir l’approbation du Congrès avant de les poursuivre. Ils s'appuyaient sur la ",["résolution sur les pouvoirs de guerre de 1973","https://www.congress.gov/bill/93rd-congress/house-joint-resolution/542"]," (War Powers Resolution)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ces ",["résolutions dites « concurrentes »","https://www.house.gov/the-house-explained/the-legislative-process/bills-resolutions"]," sont toutefois largement considérées comme ",["non contraignantes","https://www.oyez.org/cases/1981/80-1832"],". Destinées à exprimer l’opinion ou la volonté du Congrès, elles servent généralement à traiter des questions internes au Congrès."]},{"k":"p","s":["Trump l’a ignorée. Une résolution similaire a ensuite ",["échoué au Sénat","https://www.npr.org/2026/09/24/nx-s1-5980318/senate-iran-war-powers-vote"]," en septembre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pour qu’une telle résolution soit contraignante, il faudrait qu’elle ait la force d’une loi adoptée par le Congrès, à laquelle le président opposerait probablement son veto. Et pour passer outre, les démocrates auraient besoin d’une majorité des deux tiers à la fois à la Chambre des représentants et au Sénat. Il faudrait pour cela qu’un nombre important de républicains changent de camp."]},{"k":"h","s":["Exercer un contrôle"]},{"k":"p","s":["Une deuxième option pour les démocrates consiste à lancer une série d’enquêtes parlementaires sur la manière dont la guerre a été menée. Cela passerait probablement par des auditions publiques, des injonctions à comparaître ainsi que des demandes de documents adressées à l’administration Trump."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les démocrates pourraient également tenter d’engager une procédure de destitution (impeachment) contre de hauts responsables de l’administration Trump. Si Hakeem Jeffries, le démocrate pressenti pour devenir le prochain président de la Chambre des représentants, veut satisfaire certaines des voix les plus progressistes de son parti (ou les voix les plus intransigeantes sur la guerre en Iran ou contre Trump), le secrétaire à la Défense Pete Hegseth pourrait être le premier visé. Mais les motifs d’une telle procédure restent flous à ce stade, et même avec la nouvelle majorité démocrate au Sénat, il serait peu probable qu’il soit condamné, à moins qu’un nombre important de républicains ne changent de camp."]},{"k":"p","s":["Surtout, ces enquêtes parlementaires sont un processus de longue haleine, peu susceptible de mettre rapidement fin à la guerre."]},{"k":"h","s":["Le « pouvoir de la bourse »"]},{"k":"p","s":["Le pouvoir plus immédiat dont dispose le Congrès pour mettre fin rapidement à la guerre se trouve dans l’article I, section 9, de la Constitution des États-Unis, qui dispose :"]},{"k":"p","s":["Aucune somme ne sera prélevée sur le Trésor, si ce n’est en vertu de crédits ouverts par la loi […]"]},{"k":"p","s":["C’est ce que l’on appelle le « ",["pouvoir de la bourse","https://history.house.gov/Institution/Origins-Development/Power-of-the-Purse/"]," » (power of the purse)."]},{"k":"p","s":["Une fois le nouveau Congrès installé en janvier, chaque nouveau dollar que le département de la Guerre de Trump voudra dépenser devra être approuvé par la Chambre des représentants et le Sénat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Un Congrès contrôlé par les démocrates pourrait ainsi insérer dans le budget de la défense une clause interdisant d’utiliser des fonds pour des hostilités contre l’Iran. Trump pourrait y opposer son veto, mais cela reviendrait aussi à bloquer la solde de tous les militaires."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les démocrates ont tenté exactement cette approche en 2007, pour imposer un calendrier de retrait des États-Unis d’Irak. Le président de l’époque, George W. Bush, ",["y a opposé son veto","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2007/may/02/iraq.usa"],", mais la question est devenue un objet de surenchère politique, chaque camp accusant l’autre de priver les troupes états-uniennes de financement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Les démocrates ont finalement reculé face au risque croissant d’un retour de bâton de la part des électeurs. Aujourd’hui, cette approche serait tout aussi risquée. Les démocrates sont-ils prêts à mettre en jeu leur crédibilité politique si le président les accuse d’avoir laissé tomber les soldats américains ? Qui cédera le premier ?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Les républicains face à l’heure des comptes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Une fois la poussière retombée mercredi, Trump lui-même a ",["reconnu","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-05/us-midterm-elections-2026-live-updates/107257050#live-blog-post-356865"]," que la guerre en Iran avait joué un rôle dans la cuisante défaite du Parti républicain. Mais il a persisté dans sa décision, affirmant qu’il recommencerait si nécessaire pour empêcher l’Iran de se doter de l’arme nucléaire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Le vice-président J. D. Vance s’est montré moins sur la défensive. Dans une déclaration détaillée ",["publiée sur X","https://x.com/JDVance/status/2118004988433641835"],", Vance a déclaré sans détour que la guerre était la raison de la défaite des républicains. Il a ajouté : « toute conversation honnête sur la suite doit commencer par là »."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vance ",["critique depuis longtemps","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-13/jd-vance-philosophically-little-bit-different-to-me-trump-says/106449548"]," l’engagement militaire des États-Unis dans des conflits à l’étranger, mais, dans son rôle de vice-président, il a publiquement soutenu les actions de Trump contre l’Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["L’écrasante victoire démocrate de cette semaine permet désormais beaucoup plus facilement à Vance, et à d’autres républicains, de rompre avec le président."]},{"k":"h","s":["Le rapport de force a basculé"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pour Trump, mettre fin à la guerre maintenant serait une humiliation. Les États-Unis ont jusqu’ici englouti ",["près de 50 milliards de dollars","https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-costs-iran-war-rise-over-47-billion-according-pentagon-estimate-2026-10-28/"]," (environ 44 milliards d’euros) dans une campagne militaire aux résultats concrets bien maigres."]},{"k":"p","s":["De plus, l’Iran a montré que le détroit d’Ormuz est un point de passage stratégique qu’il peut contrôler. Il en va de même pour le détroit de Bab el-Mandeb, au large du Yémen, où les houthistes, alliés de l’Iran, ont attaqué des navires marchands. Ces coûts se feront sentir bien après la présidence Trump. La guerre pourrait mettre définitivement fin à l’ordre mondial unipolaire que Washington a bâti après la fin de la guerre froide. Le grand gagnant pourrait bien ne pas être Téhéran, mais Pékin."]}],"chars":7078},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tuvalu":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"cac99b9e8dd4c96101fb18d6634cc9e8e2b570c3c01edf180b900508bf20ffdb","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/tuvalu","bytes":36636,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Tuvalu travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-14T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:07:18+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide and any specific travel advice that applies to you:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["disabled travellers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["volunteering and adventure travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help British nationals make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tuvalu/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Tuvalu set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Honorary Consul for Tuvalu in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Tuvalu, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Tuvalu without a visa for up to one month."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than one month or to work, study, travel for business or other reasons, you must get an extension from the Department of Immigration in Funafuti."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Tuvalu guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/230/tuvalu#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Tuvalu","https://finance.gov.tv/customs/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Tuvalu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there is no recent history of terrorism in Tuvalu, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to import, export, cultivate or distribute drugs. Penalties include fines and imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Homosexuality is illegal in Tuvalu. If you’re found guilty of consensual sex between adult males, you could face up to 14 years in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Internet and phone services"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is one local mobile network in Tuvalu, other international networks will not work. You can buy local SIM cards in Funafuti."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no ATMs in Tuvalu, and credit or debit card payments are not accepted. Bring enough Australian dollars in cash with you for the duration of your trip."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when swimming, diving or snorkelling in the sea as currents can be extremely strong. Coral reefs can easily cause cuts and scrapes. If you decide to scuba dive, make sure you use a reputable, fully licensed company with up-to-date equipment and necessary safety features. Deaths and serious accidents have occurred because basic safety measures were not in place. There are limited medical facilities in Tuvalu."]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimming in Funafuti lagoon is not recommended as it is highly polluted."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling in any vessel, check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you’re covered by insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["it is not overloaded"]},{"k":"li","s":["there are safety precautions in place"]},{"k":"li","s":["safety equipment is accessible and in working order"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Tuvalu, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Tuvalu for up to 2 weeks. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tropical cyclone season normally runs from November to May, but cyclones can happen throughout the year. During cyclone season there is a greater risk of strong winds and heavy rains, flooding, landslides and road closures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local and international weather updates from the ",["Tuvalu Meteorological Service","https://tuvmet.tv/"],", in local newspapers and on Tuvalu Media Department Radio on 621 AM."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes and tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"]," and resulting ",["tsunamis","https://www.ready.gov/tsunamis"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 or 999 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Tuvalu","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/230/tuvalu#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Tuvalu","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/230/tuvalu#General_Information"],", including dengue."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drinking water"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink or use only boiled or bottled water and avoid ice in drinks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS has information on ",["whether you can take your medicine abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/common-health-questions/medicines/can-i-take-my-medicine-abroad/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare facilities in Tuvalu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tuvalu’s only hospital is on Funafuti. Trained nurses serve the outer islands. Medical facilities are generally adequate for routine medical treatment. For more serious or complicated problems, you may need medical evacuation to Fiji or Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance, sufficient medication supplies and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Tuvalu"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 999"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hospital: (+688) 20749"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 000"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 911"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/tuvalu/british-high-commission-suva"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tuvalu/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":9161,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"7dc7b740316aeaaef46b658286517ba28674120721280dc667c7671f282a8f92","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/usa","bytes":109609,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"USA travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-06T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-14T02:26:03+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice also covers American Samoa, Guam, Northern Mariana Islands, Puerto Rico, and United States Virgin Islands."]},{"k":"h","s":["Air traffic disruptions across the US"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) has lifted the temporary nationwide grounding of flights for all US airports. Travellers should expect some continued air travel disruptions. Check for messaging from your airline on how this will impact your travel plans and with your travel insurance provider."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have the correct approval prior to travel. This will be either a valid US visa or Electronic System for Travel Authorisation (ESTA), depending on your personal circumstances and purpose of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["US authorities enforce entry rules strictly. If you do not have the correct immigration status, or if you breach the terms of your entry, there is a risk you may be detained, refused entry, or removed (deported). Overstaying your permitted time in the US can also lead to detention and future bans on re-entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["A valid ESTA or visa does not guarantee you will be allowed to enter the US. Authorities may refuse you entry if, for example, they believe you plan to stay longer than permitted or have provided inaccurate or incomplete information. The US may change the conditions to travel to the US at any time without prior notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the US Embassy or a consulate in the UK. See information from ",["US Customs and Border Protection","https://www.cbp.gov/travel/international-visitors"]," on entry for international visitors."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter the US, your passport must be valid for the length of your planned stay."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling through another country on your way to or from the US, check the entry requirements for that country. Many countries will only allow entry if you have at least 6 months validity remaining on your passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-US dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["US law requires US citizens to enter and exit the US using a US passport. Contact the ",["US Embassy or a consulate in the UK","https://uk.usembassy.gov/"]," for more information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter or transit through the US, you must have either an ",["Electronic System for Travel Authorisation (ESTA)","https://esta.cbp.dhs.gov/"]," or a ",["visa","https://uk.usembassy.gov/visas/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US State Department has ",["more information on visas","https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers whose sex on their passport differs from their sex recorded at birth should contact ",["the US Embassy or a consulate","https://uk.usembassy.gov/"]," in the UK for further advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for an ESTA"]},{"k":"p","s":["ESTA is an automated system that determines the eligibility of visitors to travel to the US under the Visa Waiver Program (VWP). You can apply for an ESTA via the ",["Official ESTA Application Website","https://esta.cbp.dhs.gov/"]," or using the ",["ESTA Mobile app on android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=gov.dhs.cbp.esta&hl=en&gl=gb"]," or ",["on iOS","https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/esta-mobile/id1529604353"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["All Visa Waiver Program (VWP) travellers intending to enter the US by land, sea and air will be required to obtain an approved ESTA prior to application for admission at land border ports of entry. Individuals who are not eligible to travel under the VWP may apply for a visa at any ",["U.S. Embassy & Consulates","https://uk.usembassy.gov/embassy-consulates/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You may not be able to apply for an ESTA visa waiver if you have:"]},{"k":"li","s":["been arrested (even if the arrest did not result in a criminal conviction)"]},{"k":"li","s":["a criminal record"]},{"k":"li","s":["been refused admission into, or have been deported from, the US"]},{"k":"li","s":["previously overstayed under an ESTA visa waiver"]},{"k":"p","s":["Information on whether you are eligible for an ESTA visa waiver can be found in the help section of the ",["official ESTA Application Website","https://esta.cbp.dhs.gov/faq?lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot normally apply for an ESTA visa waiver if you were in the following countries on or after March 2011:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Iran"]},{"k":"li","s":["Iraq"]},{"k":"li","s":["Libya"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Korea"]},{"k":"li","s":["Somalia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sudan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Syria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Yemen"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot apply for an ESTA visa waiver if you travelled to or were in Cuba on or after 12 January 2021."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your ESTA does not contain the required selfie photograph now required by US Customs and Border Protection, you may need to apply for a new ESTA. You should check your ESTA account before travelling to ensure your authorisation remains valid."]},{"k":"p","s":["An ESTA may not be sufficient for all types of business travel – particularly if you are travelling on behalf of a US company. Please check the rules on the ",["ESTA website","https://esta.cbp.dhs.gov/"]," carefully."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are not eligible for an ESTA, you must instead apply for a US visa. Travelling on an ESTA when ineligible can lead to detention and deportation by the US authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Embassy in London has information on ",["how to apply for a visa","https://uk.usembassy.gov/visas/"],". Please check the guidance carefully."]},{"k":"hs","s":["US visa appointments"]},{"k":"p","s":["Visa appointments at the US Embassy in London are limited. Plan your application as far ahead as possible before travel. If you need to travel urgently, you can request an expedited interview through the US Embassy’s appointment service provider."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Embassy has more ",["information on visa appointments","https://uk.usembassy.gov/visas/u-s-visa-and-travel-faqs/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Children and young people"]},{"k":"p","s":["Anyone aged 17 and under must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a valid visa or ESTA on arrival"]},{"k":"li","s":["be able to provide evidence about the purpose, location and length of their visit if asked by immigration officials"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a letter of consent, preferably in English and notarised from one or both parents if travelling alone, with only one parent, or with someone who is not a parent or legal guardian"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US authorities can stop you entering the country if they have safeguarding concerns about a child. If this happens, the US authorities will take the child into their care, and their return from the US could take months. The FCDO cannot speed up the return of British nationals aged 17 and under from the US."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US government has ",["information about children travelling to the US","https://www.usa.gov/travel-documents-children"],". If you have questions, contact the ",["US Embassy in the UK","https://uk.usembassy.gov/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s US guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/235/usa#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) has ",["declared a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"]," in the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC) and Uganda."]},{"k":"p","s":["From 3 November 2026, if you are flying to or transiting through the US you must complete and sign a form before boarding their flight. The form asks you to confirm whether you have been in the DRC in the 21 days before your flight. Read more about the requirements on the ",["Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) website","https://www.cdc.gov/index.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your airline for advice about the process for completing the form before you travel. You may not be allowed to board if you do not complete the form."]},{"k":"p","s":["For passengers under 18, a parent, guardian or other authorised person must complete and sign the form on their behalf."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are also temporary US entry restrictions for some people who have recently been in the DRC, Uganda or South Sudan. Check the guidance for ",["travellers from Ebola-affected areas","https://www.cdc.gov/ebola/situation-summary/returning-travelers.html?CDC_AA_refVal=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cdc.gov%2Febola%2Fsituation-summary%2Ftitle-42-order.html"]," before you travel and contact your airline if you are unsure about the rules."]},{"k":"h","s":["Electronic devices"]},{"k":"p","s":["Officials may ask to inspect your electronic devices, emails, text messages, and social media activity. If you refuse, they can delay or deny your entry. US Customs and Border Protection has ",["more information on electronic device searches","https://www.cbp.gov/travel/cbp-search-authority/border-search-electronic-devices"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of the US","https://www.cbp.gov/travel/us-citizens/know-before-you-go/prohibited-and-restricted-items"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Global Entry"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Customs and Border Protection Trusted Traveller Program (TTP) Global Entry allows pre-approved, low-risk travellers expedited clearance at some US airports. If you’re a British citizen, you can ",["register to get a UK background check","https://www.gov.uk/apply-faster-entry-usa"],". If you pass the background checks, you’ll be invited to apply for ",["Global Entry for UK Citizens","https://www.cbp.gov/travel/trusted-traveler-programs/global-entry/international-arrangements/UnitedKingdom/global-entry-UK-citizens"],". Check eligibility carefully."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in the USA"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try and carry out attacks in the US."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by tourists and foreign nationals such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places and mass gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["transportation networks"]},{"k":"li","s":["sporting and cultural events"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship and religious sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["hospitals and clinics, schools and universities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities. The US Department of Homeland Security provides alerts within the US and its territories. If there is a life threatening emergency, call 911. US authorities regularly report that they have disrupted planned attacks and made arrests. ",["Report suspicious activity","https://www.dhs.gov/report-suspicious-activity#:~:text=If%20you%20see%20suspicious%20activity%2C%20please%20report%20it,assess%20the%20situation%2C%20they%20can%20obtain%20additional%20support."]," to local law enforcement authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not leave passports in rental cars, especially not in the boot. Gangs may target vehicles driven by people who look like tourists."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent crime and gun crime rarely affect tourists, but take care in unfamiliar areas. Try not to walk through quieter areas alone, especially at night. You can find public advisories and information about recent incidents on local law enforcement websites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mass shooting incidents can happen but are a very small percentage of murders. The US Department of Homeland Security has advice on ",["what to do in an active shooter incident","https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools/resources/active-shooter-pocket-card"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research your destination before you travel and follow the advice of local authorities. Crime linked to illegal drugs is a major issue in Mexican states bordering Arizona, California, New Mexico and Texas. Some foreign nationals have been victims of crime in the border regions, but there is no evidence they were targeted because of their nationality."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests are common and can become violent. Follow the instructions of local authorities who may introduce curfews or emergency orders. If you attend peaceful protests or mass gatherings:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be mindful of your surroundings"]},{"k":"li","s":["move away if there are signs of trouble"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the instructions of local authorities"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["US states may have different laws. While you are in a state, you are subject to both that state’s laws as well as national (federal) law. Not adhering to all US state and federal law can put your visa status and future travel to the US at risk."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry a passport showing you have permission to enter or remain in the US."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["The national legal age for buying and drinking alcohol is 21 across the US."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through airports. US law prohibits the importation, exportation, manufacture, sale or transportation of drug paraphernalia. If you are convicted of any of these offenses, you will be subject to fines and imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in USA have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers. All persons arriving at a port-of-entry to the United States are subject to inspection by U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) officers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check state laws to make sure you follow laws on possession and use of controlled substances. The US Department of Justice provides a ",["list of all controlled substances","https://www.dea.gov/drug-information/csa"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US is a very diverse society and attitudes towards LGBT+ people differ hugely across the country. Check state and local laws for the areas you plan to travel to. Refer to entry requirements which may apply to LGBT+ travellers (see ",["entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa/entry-requirements"],")."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor Activities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re taking part in organised outdoor activities, check that the company is reputable and has documented safety procedures."]},{"k":"p","s":["For sports activities like skiing, potholing and mountaineering, and for sports classed as particularly dangerous (for example off-piste skiing, mountain biking, climbing or paragliding), your insurance should include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mountain rescue services"]},{"k":"li","s":["helicopter costs"]},{"k":"li","s":["repatriation to your country of residence or possible transfer to neighbouring countries for treatment"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking"]},{"k":"li","s":["Check weather forecasts and conditions and make sure you’re properly equipped for the worst-case scenario with items such as a map, compass, GPS and telecommunication equipment."]},{"k":"li","s":["Risks are greater if you undertake any activity alone. You may want to hire a guide for expert advice. Always leave copies of your itinerary with someone."]},{"k":"li","s":["Check the ",["US National Park Service website","https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.nps.gov%2Fsubjects%2Fhealthandsafety%2Fprepare-for-your-activity.htm&data=05%7C02%7CCharlotte.Nixon%40fcdo.gov.uk%7C5608e46cd9ad40b0d00108ddb3cd1a56%7Cd3a2d0d37cc84f52bbf985bd43d94279%7C0%7C0%7C638864415742509094%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=uYGfw4%2FbGIrOmgHe0FyTSaiwHA378PKZDfZiVbQIn74%3D&reserved=0"]," for additional advice."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Winter sports"]},{"k":"li","s":["Read about ",["preparing for winter sports abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/winter-sports-stay-safe-on-the-slopes"],"."]},{"k":"li","s":["Take advice on weather and avalanche conditions before you travel. Follow local skiing laws and regulations."]},{"k":"li","s":["Off-piste skiing is very dangerous and can invalidate your travel insurance. Avalanches are a risk in some areas. Follow safety instructions carefully and go with a qualified guide. Check ahead on the ",["National Avalanche Center website","https://avalanche.org/#/current"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in the US, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the driving rules in the states you’ll be visiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in the US. You may need to get the ",["1949 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well. IDP requirements vary in each state. For more information, consult individual states’ ",["Department of Motor Vehicles","https://www.usa.gov/state-motor-vehicle-services"]," as well as the ",["American Automobile Association (AAA)","https://www.aaa.com/International/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you still have a paper driving licence, you must take another form of photo ID, such as your passport. You can also ",["exchange your paper driving licence for a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by car, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check weather conditions before a long car journey, particularly in mountainous, isolated or desert areas where services may be limited"]},{"k":"li","s":["not sleep in your car by the road or in rest areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid leaving any items on display in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay on main roads"]},{"k":"li","s":["use well-lit car parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in an accident, ask any other drivers involved to follow you to a public place and call the police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Petrol stations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Petrol stations that do not display the price of fuel usually charge considerably more than the national average. They’re often close to tourist destinations and airports. Make sure you know the price of fuel before using these services."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel, check the security measures you’re likely to face at the airport on the Transportation Security Administration (TSA) website. If you have a medical condition or disability and need assistance, ",["contact TSA Cares","https://www.tsa.gov/travel/passenger-support#:~:text=TSA%20offers%20screening%20information%20and,need%20additional%20assistance%20with%20screening."],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["To monitor airport conditions in the US, check the Federal Aviation Administration website."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Snowstorms"]},{"k":"p","s":["Snowstorms can disrupt critical infrastructure, and cause power cuts, or delays and cancellations in major transport hubs. Contact your travel company or airline before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Atlantic hurricane season normally runs from June to November. The Pacific hurricane season normally runs from May to November. Hurricanes can affect coastal regions, Hawaii and Guam. The South Pacific tropical cyclone season normally runs from November to May and can affect American Samoa."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["US National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration’s","https://www.noaa.gov/"]," (NOAA) seasonal outlook predicts a “below-normal Atlantic hurricane season” and an “above-normal hurricane season in the central Pacific basin”, including the waters around Hawaii in 2026. Travellers to the USA during hurricane season should check the websites of local, State and Federal agencies (such as NOAA and the ",["US National Hurricane Center","https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/"],") for the latest forecasts and conditions. You should also be aware of the possibility of disruption to flights and other transport services."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor approaching storms on the ",["US National Hurricane Center website","https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow instructions from local authorities, including evacuation orders"]},{"k":"li","s":["visit the ",["Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) website","https://www.fema.gov/"]," for information on preparing for extreme weather and evacuatingCheck with your airline or travel agent about possible disruption to flights or airport services and follow their advice"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["While earthquakes can happen anywhere without warning in the US, Alaska, California, Hawaii, Oregon, Puerto Rico, Washington and the entire Mississippi River Valley are at higher risk for earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The FEMA website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tornadoes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tornadoes can happen anytime depending on weather conditions. The FEMA website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after a tornado","https://www.ready.gov/tornadoes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is volcanic activity across parts of the US with Alaska, Hawaii, California, Washington and Oregon having the largest number of active volcanoes. You should follow the advice of local authorities, including any evacuation orders."]},{"k":"p","s":["The FEMA website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after a volcanic eruption","https://www.ready.gov/volcanoes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Forest and brush fires (wildfires) are a danger in many dry areas, particularly in canyons, hills and forests. High winds can mean fires spread rapidly."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media and ",["weather reports","https://www.noaa.gov/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities, including any evacuation orders"]},{"k":"li","s":["be careful in areas recently affected by wildfires, as there may be mudslides during heavy rainfall"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information visit the ",["National Interagency Fire Center","https://www.nifc.gov/"]," and ",["Fire Research and Management Exchange System","https://www.frames.gov/"]," websites."]},{"k":"p","s":["For information about wildfires in California, see the ",["CAL FIRE","https://www.fire.ca.gov/incidents/"]," website."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flash flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash floods can cause travel disruption and damage to property and infrastructure. ",["Check weather warnings from the US’s National Weather Service (NOAA)","https://eur03.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.weather.gov%2Falerts%2Fas.htmlThere&data=05%7C02%7CCharlotte.Nixon%40fcdo.gov.uk%7C9a8c32ec8cb642ebb07708ddbd320a1b%7Cd3a2d0d37cc84f52bbf985bd43d94279%7C0%7C0%7C638874745075644264%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=mF0mOSTmh1SeiMrQlYfUJ4AjItXBkRv7%2Fh%2BZkLYgs0U%3D&reserved=0"]," before travel and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arctic travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Parts of the US are in the Arctic Circle, including some very remote areas of land and sea. Emergency medical assistance and search and rescue are limited in these areas. See ",["Arctic travel safety advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/arctic-travel-safety-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for the US","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/235/usa#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," (or the ",["US Virgin Islands","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/242/virgin-islands-usa#Vaccine_Recommendations"],", ",["Puerto Rico","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/182/puerto-rico#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and ",["American Samoa, Guam and the Northern Mariana Islands","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/263/american-samoa-guam-northern-mariana-islands#Vaccine_Recommendations"],")"]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in the US","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/235/usa#General_Information"]," (or the ",["US Virgin Islands","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/242/virgin-islands-usa#General_Information"],", ",["Puerto Rico","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/182/puerto-rico#General_Information"]," and ",["American Samoa, Guam and the Northern Mariana Islands","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/263/american-samoa-guam-northern-mariana-islands#General_Information"],"), including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["West Nile virus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of the US. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take some prescription drugs into the US. The US Food and Drug Administration provides information on ",["bringing medicines into the US","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/cder/daf/index.cfm"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK prescriptions are not valid in the US. To get pharmacy drugs, you need a prescription from a US provider (available from an urgent care facility, emergency room or a doctor)."]},{"k":"p","s":["TravelHealthPro explains ",["best practice when travelling with medicines","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS has information on ",["whether you can take your medicine abroad","https://www.nhs.uk/common-health-questions/medicines/can-i-take-my-medicine-abroad/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in the US"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical treatment is expensive and there are no special arrangements for British visitors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some hospitals ask non-US residents to pay a deposit when admitted. Send any requests for funds to your travel insurance provider first; only pay the hospital if you’re advised to do so by your travel insurance company. Your medical care will not be affected while your claim is processed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities in American Samoa are basic and you may need medical evacuation by air ambulance to Hawaii, New Zealand or Australia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in the US"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=United%20States"]," in the US"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in the US","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-for-the-usa"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in the US","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/usa-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you are ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/usa/british-embassy-washington"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":23470,"change":"Updated information on air traffic disruptions across the US"},"https://theconversation.com/corruption-in-south-africas-police-force-is-rife-why-protecting-whistleblowers-is-vital-295357":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"e9f9197e382f65e5424cbad07d58896ca5524b6e96b9f05178e076a54e1bd099","read":"https://theconversation.com/corruption-in-south-africas-police-force-is-rife-why-protecting-whistleblowers-is-vital-295357","bytes":179729,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Corruption in South Africa’s police force is rife: why protecting whistleblowers is vital","by":[{"n":"Azwihangwisi Judith Mphidi","r":"Adjunct Academic, University of South Africa"}],"pub":"2026-10-29T14:03:23Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["South African Police Service members who act with integrity sometimes suffer for it. If they witness corruption, refuse to participate in misconduct, or raise a grievance, they may be labelled disloyal, excluded from professional networks, denied promotion, transferred to undesirable posts, or pressured to leave the service."]},{"k":"p","s":["These are not hypothetical concerns. ",["An interim report","https://www.polity.org.za/article/ramaphosa-receives-interim-report-of-madlanga-commission-2025-12-18"]," released by the ",["Madlanga Commission of Inquiry","https://criminaljusticecommission.org.za/"]," named 14 senior police and Ekurhuleni (municipal) officials for investigation into alleged corruption and political interference. South African president Cyril Ramaphosa established the commission in 2025 to look into criminality, political interference and corruption in the criminal justice system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public hearings have ",["heard allegations that corruption has reached senior levels of policing","https://www.sanews.gov.za/south-africa/president-ramaphosa-acts-saps-and-ekurhuleni-officials-named-madlanga-interim-report"],". At the ",["2026 SAPS Fraud and Corruption Imbizo","https://www.unisa.ac.za/sites/corporate/default/Colleges/Law/News-&-events/Articles/Imbizo-targets-fraud-and-corruption-on-a-national-scale"],", a meeting convened at the University of South Africa (Unisa) in response to the commission’s findings, officers and delegates described fear, resignation and the normalisation of silence after reporting wrongdoing."]},{"k":"p","s":["It reflects a broader South African pattern. Corruption Watch, a not-for-profit anti-corruption agency, has ",["documented","https://www.corruptionwatch.org.za/sa-whistleblowers-face-retaliation-and-murder-their-stories-over-five-decades/"]," five decades of whistleblowers facing dismissal, intimidation, social isolation and even murder. Not every case involves the police. Nevertheless, it shows that disclosure without credible institutional protection can carry severe personal and professional costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["I research ethical policing, corruption, accountability and governance reform. As a participant and observer at the discussions at Unisa, I heard repeated concerns about retaliation, fear of disclosure, distrust of reporting channels and the perception that management protected its own. This raised a central question: surely these events could not be treated as an ordinary workplace issue? If police members feared punishment for reporting corruption, how could the police service credibly confront corruption within its own ranks?"]},{"k":"p","s":["In a recent paper I ",["argue","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/10246029.2026.2728585"]," that the state has a constitutional duty to protect members of the South African Police Service from internal retaliation. And failing to do so allows corruption to continue harming the communities that police are meant to serve."]},{"k":"p","s":["I argue that protecting police members is not simply a workplace welfare issue. It is a constitutional obligation. Where the police service tolerates retaliation against ethical officers, it weakens the institutional integrity required to confront corruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["I propose a protection model based on three pillars:"]},{"k":"li","s":["police members have rights"]},{"k":"li","s":["the state has a duty to make those rights effective"]},{"k":"li","s":["protecting members is a precondition for human security."]},{"k":"h","s":["On the ground"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Retaliation","https://issafrica.org/iss-today/breaking-the-code-of-silence-is-key-to-confronting-sa-police-corruption"]," within the police service is often informal and difficult to prove. It takes forms like stalled promotions, undesirable transfers, exclusion from professional networks, reputational labelling and pressure to resign rather than dismissal."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research","https://www.researchgate.net/publication/401019210_Discipline_Restoration_Procedures_in_the_South_African_Police_Service_Challenges_and_Effective_Responses"]," has also identified four reinforcing dynamics that produce silence: fear of retaliation, loyalty pressures, moral rationalisation and distrust of reporting channels."]},{"k":"p","s":["On top of this, research on whistleblowing ",["consistently shows","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/business-ethics-quarterly/article/abs/making-sense-of-whistleblowings-antecedents-learning-from-research-on-identity-and-ethics-programs/B71183EB745A188F4209EFB306AF8EAA"]," that people who report wrongdoing may face retaliation, isolation, career damage and threats to their safety, even where formal protections exist. Employees are more likely to remain silent where disclosure might threaten their standing, relationships or career prospects."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research also ",["finds","https://mumabusinessreview.org/2020/MBR-04-10-107-118-Breckon-RetaliatoryBehavior.pdf"]," that retaliation is less likely where organisations build cultures of trust, respect, collective identity and justice."]},{"k":"p","s":["This has direct implications for the South African Police Service. Legal rules alone cannot protect officers if the everyday culture rewards loyalty to corrupt networks over fidelity to the law."]},{"k":"p","s":["In South Africa, the risks are severe. Corruption Watch has ",["documented","https://www.corruptionwatch.org.za/using-the-law-to-frustrate-rather-than-support-whistle-blowers/"]," how legal processes can be used to frustrate rather than support whistleblowers. Its ",["later research","https://www.corruptionwatch.org.za/sa-whistleblowers-face-retaliation-and-murder-their-stories-over-five-decades/"]," records decades of retaliation against people who exposed corruption. It included intimidation, dismissal, social isolation and murder."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings show that whistleblower protection cannot depend only on legislation. It requires enforcement, independence and institutional willingness to act."]},{"k":"p","s":["The “blue wall of silence” within policing adds another layer. ",["Research","https://academic.oup.com/policing/article/doi/10.1093/police/paae032/7614892"]," shows that loyalty, fear of professional consequences and norms of solidarity can discourage officers from reporting misconduct. This culture can turn whistleblowing from a professional duty into a perceived betrayal. Officers may fear being called a “snitch”, losing informal support, or being treated as an enemy by colleagues and supervisors."]},{"k":"h","s":["The cost of silence"]},{"k":"p","s":["The consequences of silence are not abstract. Wrongdoing becomes harder to expose. Corrupt networks are protected. Accountability is delayed. Communities continue to experience organised crime, drug trafficking and weakened policing."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Afrobarometer (2024)","https://www.afrobarometer.org/"]," reports that South Africans’ views of the police are shaped by perceived corruption and low trust."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research ",["shows","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0306624X20928019"]," that police corruption undermines public trust and that procedural fairness is central to rebuilding confidence in policing. Communities are not simply reacting emotionally to isolated scandals. They are responding rationally to repeated institutional failure."]},{"k":"p","s":["The discussions at Unisa reflected this connection. Participants linked internal corruption to drug proliferation and community insecurity. Where officers are silenced, harm extends from the individual whistleblower to families, schools, neighbourhoods and future opportunities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protection must come first"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Africa cannot ask officers to report corruption while leaving them exposed to retaliation. This is especially serious where reports involve senior officials or where reporting channels are in the same chain of command being complained about."]},{"k":"p","s":["Reform must begin with credible protection. The South African Police Force and the Independent Police Investigative Directorate should establish secure, anonymised reporting channels that are independent of local command structures. Disclosures involving senior officials should receive priority and be insulated from those involved."]},{"k":"p","s":["The law should also recognise informal retaliation more clearly. The police service could be required to show that adverse treatment was unrelated to a disclosure."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ethics training should reframe whistleblowing as a constitutional and professional duty rather than disloyalty. Officers who disclose wrongdoing should receive immediate legal and psycho-social support."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, the Madlanga Commission’s recommendations must be carried out visibly, with regular public reporting, so communities can see accountability."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public anger towards the police is understandable. But broad distrust also unfairly affects the many officers who serve with integrity. The way to distinguish between a police service with a corruption problem and a corrupt institution is visible accountability."]},{"k":"p","s":["That accountability begins inside the organisation."]}],"chars":7039}};
